{
  "summary": "Updates `analyzepsbt` to flag PSBTs whose output values exceed input values as invalid once all input amounts are known. Instead of reporting a negative fee and setting the next role to updater or signer, the RPC now returns an error string and suggests creator as the next role.",
  "problem": "When all inputs are known but total outputs exceed total inputs, `analyzepsbt` calculates a negative fee and suggests downstream roles like updater or signer for a transaction that can never be signed or broadcast validly.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'AnalyzePSBT computes fee = in_amt - out_amt once every input amount is known and returns it as is. A PSBT whose outputs are worth more than its inputs therefore gets a negative fee and a next role of updater, even though no wallet can ever sign it into a valid transaction.'",
    "Commit 8262933013: 'When every input amount is known, AnalyzePSBT computed fee as in_amt - out_amt and returned it even if it was negative, together with a negative fee rate and a next role of updater or signer. Treat a PSBT that pays out more than it spends as invalid, like the other amount checks in the same function.'"
